<h2 id="faq-heading">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<div class="usa-accordion usa-accordion--bordered usa-accordion--multiselectable" data-allow-multiple="">
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="faq-1">What is product handling on a conveyor?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-1" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>Turning, flipping, orienting, inverting, or repositioning products on a conveyor to achieve correct position for downstream operations. Devices operate inline without stopping flow.</p>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-2">What is a product turner?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-2" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>Rotates products around a vertical axis (90 or 180 degrees) using angled belts, guide rails, servo turntables, or <a href="/conveyor-types/transfer-conveyors/">right-angle transfers</a>. Used for label positioning, case pattern formation, and scanner access.</p>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-3">What is product inversion?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-3" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>Flips product 180 degrees around a horizontal axis. Uses twist belts, clamping inverters, overhead flippers, or gravity inversion. Applications: bottle air-rinse, bottom labeling/coding, tray depanning, and drainage.</p>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-4">How do you orient products on a conveyor?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-4" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>Passive methods use product geometry and guide rails. Active methods use vision cameras to detect orientation and servo turntables or robots to correct misoriented products. Vision-guided robots handle the widest range of shapes, at rates set by the product and gripper.</p>

</div>
